# Standards de Tests

## Principes généraux

- **AAA Pattern** : Arrange, Act, Assert
- **Un test = un comportement** : pas de tests qui testent plusieurs choses
- **Noms descriptifs** : should_return_user_when_valid_id
- **Indépendance** : les tests ne dépendent pas les uns des autres
- **Déterministes** : même résultat à chaque exécution

## Jest / Vitest (JavaScript/TypeScript)

### Structure

```typescript
// Mock dependencies BEFORE imports
jest.mock('../api/userService', () => ({
  fetchUser: jest.fn(),
}));

import { fetchUser } from '../api/userService';
import { getUserData } from '../utils/userUtils';

describe('getUserData', () => {
  beforeEach(() => {
    jest.clearAllMocks();
  });

  it('should return user data when fetch is successful', async () => {
    // Arrange
    const mockUser = { id: 1, name: 'John' };
    (fetchUser as jest.Mock).mockResolvedValue(mockUser);

    // Act
    const result = await getUserData(1);

    // Assert
    expect(result).toEqual(mockUser);
    expect(fetchUser).toHaveBeenCalledWith(1);
  });

  it('should throw error when user not found', async () => {
    // Arrange
    (fetchUser as jest.Mock).mockRejectedValue(new Error('Not found'));

    // Act & Assert
    await expect(getUserData(999)).rejects.toThrow('Not found');
  });
});
```

### Bonnes pratiques Jest

```typescript
// ✅ Describe nested pour organisation
describe('UserService', () => {
  describe('createUser', () => {
    describe('with valid data', () => {
      it('should create and return user', async () => {});
    });

    describe('with invalid data', () => {
      it('should throw validation error', async () => {});
    });
  });
});

// ✅ Test data factories
const createMockUser = (overrides = {}) => ({
  id: '1',
  name: 'John Doe',
  email: 'john@example.com',
  ...overrides,
});

// ✅ Snapshot testing pour UI
it('should render correctly', () => {
  const { container } = render(<UserCard user={mockUser} />);
  expect(container).toMatchSnapshot();
});
```

## Playwright (E2E)

### Structure

```typescript
import { test, expect } from '@playwright/test';

test.describe('Login Page', () => {
  test.beforeEach(async ({ page }) => {
    // Mock API
    await page.route('/api/login', (route) => {
      const body = route.request().postDataJSON();
      if (body.email === 'valid@test.com') {
        route.fulfill({
          status: 200,
          body: JSON.stringify({ token: 'fake-token' }),
        });
      } else {
        route.fulfill({
          status: 401,
          body: JSON.stringify({ error: 'Invalid credentials' }),
        });
      }
    });

    await page.goto('/login');
  });

  test('should login with valid credentials', async ({ page }) => {
    await page.getByTestId('email').fill('valid@test.com');
    await page.getByTestId('password').fill('password123');
    await page.getByTestId('submit').click();

    await expect(page.getByTestId('dashboard')).toBeVisible();
  });

  test('should show error for invalid credentials', async ({ page }) => {
    await page.getByTestId('email').fill('invalid@test.com');
    await page.getByTestId('password').fill('wrong');
    await page.getByTestId('submit').click();

    await expect(page.getByTestId('error-message')).toHaveText('Invalid credentials');
  });
});
```

### Sélecteurs Playwright

```typescript
// ✅ Priorité des sélecteurs (du meilleur au pire)
page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Submit' })  // 1. Rôle accessible
page.getByTestId('submit-button')              // 2. Test ID
page.getByText('Submit')                       // 3. Texte visible
page.locator('button.submit')                  // 4. CSS (éviter)
```

## pytest (Python)

### Structure

```python
import pytest
from unittest.mock import Mock, patch

class TestUserService:
    @pytest.fixture
    def user_service(self):
        return UserService(repository=Mock())

    @pytest.fixture
    def mock_user(self):
        return User(id="1", name="John", email="john@test.com")

    def test_get_user_returns_user_when_found(
        self, user_service, mock_user
    ):
        # Arrange
        user_service.repository.find_by_id.return_value = mock_user

        # Act
        result = user_service.get("1")

        # Assert
        assert result == mock_user
        user_service.repository.find_by_id.assert_called_once_with("1")

    def test_get_user_raises_when_not_found(self, user_service):
        # Arrange
        user_service.repository.find_by_id.return_value = None

        # Act & Assert
        with pytest.raises(NotFoundError):
            user_service.get("999")


# Parametrized tests
@pytest.mark.parametrize("input,expected", [
    ("", False),
    ("invalid", False),
    ("valid@email.com", True),
])
def test_is_valid_email(input, expected):
    assert is_valid_email(input) == expected
```

## Couverture de tests

| Type | Quoi tester | Proportion |
|------|-------------|------------|
| **Unit** | Fonctions pures, utils, services | 70% |
| **Integration** | API endpoints, DB queries | 20% |
| **E2E** | Parcours utilisateur critiques | 10% |

## Checklist tests

- [ ] Noms descriptifs (should_do_X_when_Y)
- [ ] Pattern AAA respecté
- [ ] Mocks nettoyés entre tests (beforeEach)
- [ ] Edge cases couverts (null, undefined, empty)
- [ ] Erreurs testées
- [ ] Tests indépendants et déterministes
- [ ] Pas de tests de styles visuels
